r.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-01-01\nValid as Of: 2025-08-12\nVersion: 3.12\n\n--- Record 323 ---\nComponent: Decentralized Identity Verification\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Improvement of the Company Identity Status Check\nDescription: For Decentralized Identity Verification-hosted identities, the company identity status can be updated immediately.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-01-01\nValid as Of: 2025-08-12\nVersion: 3.12\n\n--- Record 324 ---\nComponent: Decentralized Identity Verification\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Retrieval of Shared Verifiable Presentation using Access Token\nDescription: Verifiers can now retry the retrieval of a shared verifiable presentation using a valid access token multiple times until the token expires, rather than a single retrieval attempt as before.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-01-01\nValid as Of: 2025-08-12\nVersion: 3.12\n\n--- Record 325 ---\nComponent: Identity Provisioning\nEnvironment: Neo\nTitle: Mandatory email for job subscribers\nDescription: A message in the UI now ensures that all subscribers for job notifications provide an email address.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-08-12\nValid as Of: 2025-08-12\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 326 ---\nComponent: Graph\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Try out GraphQL Queries in the Graph Navigator on the Developer Hub\nDescription: You can try out GraphQL queries in the Graph Navigator on the Developer Hub. For more information, see Graph Navigator on Developer Hub.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Intelligent Technologies\nLatest Revision: 2025-08-11\nValid as Of: 2025-08-11\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 327 ---\nComponent: Kyma Runtime\nEnvironment: Kyma\nTitle: Istio module: Update to version 1.20.2\nDescription: Version 1.20.2 introduces the following improvements:      The Istio module now supports the use of Istio sidecars as Kubernetes init containers. In addition to the default Istio containers, the module also restarts native sidecar init containers. However, configuring native sidecars directly from the Istio Custom Resource (CR) is not supported. For more information, see issue #1426.Caution  If your cluster's Istio service mesh includes workloads with initContainer sidecars, the Istio module will restart these workloads for the first time. See Restart of Workloads with Enabled Istio Sidecar Injection, Istio sidecar documentation, and Kubernetes Native Sidecars in Istio.    We've updated the Istio version to 1.26.2. For more information, read the Istio 1.26.2 release announcement and Istio 1.26.0 release announcement.  We've fixed a bug where the proxy-protocol EnvoyFilter applied by the Istio module on AWS clusters with ELB load balancers was incorrectly detected as a user resource. This resulted in the Istio custom resource being set to the Warning state. See issue #1491.  We've fixed a bug where labels of the Istio managed resources were not correctly reconciled.  We've fixed a bug where the app.kubernetes.io/version label was not set to the proper version in the managed resources.  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-07-22\nValid as Of: 2025-08-11\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 328 ---\nComponent: SAP Document AI\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Integration of SAP Document AI (Embedded Edition) with SAP Mobile Start\nDescription: You can now integrate SAP Document AI with SAP Mobile Start. The integration lets you use your mobile device to upload documents or scan printed documents and then upload the resulting images for automatic information extraction.  See Integrating SAP Document AI With Your SAP Solution (Embedded Edition and Premium Edition).\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Intelligent Technologies\nLatest Revision: 2025-09-04\nValid as Of: 2025-08-11\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 329 ---\nComponent: Cloud Integration\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Neo\nTitle: ELSTER Adapter Supports New ERiC Version\nDescription: A new version 42.2.2.0 of the Elster Rich Client (ERiC) library is available for the ELSTER adapter.   This update includes enhanced data type versions\",508\n688,\"--- Record 1521 ---\nComponent: Cloud Identity Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo\nTitle: Provisioning sub-attributes of emails attribute\nDescription: Changes in the read transformations of Identity Authentication (version 1 and 2), Local Identity Directory, and SAP Ariba Invoice Management ensure that Identity Provisioning now reads all sub-attributes of the emails attribute as defined in the SCIM core schema (that is, value, type, primary, display).  Changes in the write and proxy write transformations of Identity Authentication (version 2) ensure that users with multiple email addresses are provisioned with the correct primary email.  For more information, see Identity Authentication (Source), Identity Authentication (Target), Identity Authentication (Proxy).\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-01-29\nValid as Of: 2025-01-29\nVersion: 27344\n\n--- Record 1522 ---\nComponent: Cloud Identity Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo\nTitle: Reduced Set of Scopes for Credentials of Cloud Identity Services Instances\nDescription: When you create a new binding or service key for a service instance of Cloud Identity Services with the application plan, the generated credential only has the following scopes depending on the credential type:      Certificates: OpenID and Identity Directory for Applications.      Secrets and JSON Web Key Sets: OpenID.      If the application needs additional scopes, such as Application or Application Users, the tenant administrator must explicitly grant them.  For more information about configuring client credentials, see Configure Secrets for API Authentication.  For more information about using SAP Cloud Identity Services with SAP BTP, see Integrating the Service with the Identity Service of SAP BTP.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-01-29\nValid as Of: 2025-01-29\nVersion: 27344\n\n--- Record 1523 ---\nComponent: Cloud Identity Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo\nTitle: Regular Upgrade\nDescription: Cloud Identity Services have been upgraded.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-01-29\nValid as Of: 2025-01-29\nVersion: 27344\n\n--- Record 1524 ---\nComponent: Continuous Integration & Delivery\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Sporadic Internal Server Errors Resolved\nDescription: A temporary issue that caused failed operations in the service user interface has been resolved.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-01-29\nValid as Of: 2025-01-29\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1525 ---\nComponent: Decentralized Identity Verification\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Sign Revocation Lists\nDescription: A revocation list can now be signed, and its signature is validated during verification.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-01-01\nValid as Of: 2025-01-29\nVersion: 3.6\n\n--- Record 1526 ---\nComponent: Identity Provisioning\nEnvironment: Neo\nTitle: Group mapping changes\nDescription: The default read and proxy read transformations of SAP Ariba Applications and SAP Ana